// === PREAMBLE ===
// @trope    Hope Bringer
// @category Heroes / Character
// @source   https://allthetropes.org/wiki/Hope_Bringer
// @domain   Narrative
// @version  1.3
//
// Laconic (per the wiki): living proof that one figure can make a difference and even the odds —
// by his deeds and his very presence he restores hope in the hearts of his allies and leads the
// broken back into the fight and to victory. FRONTIER: the FIGURE who is the exact inverse of the
// Despair Event Horizon. Where the horizon takes a hopeful character and makes despair ABSOLUTE,
// the Hope Bringer takes the [#Despairing] and turns them [#Hopeful] / [+Resolved] — restoration
// where the horizon was foreclosure. Distinct from the Rousing Speech: that is the SPEECH ACT (an
// orator turning a [#Disheartened] band's fear with words, cause + band); this is the ROLE — the
// beacon restores by PRESENCE and DEEDS, not by oratory, and the figure himself IS the argument.


// === IMPORTS & ASSOCIATIONS ===
import "trl/concepts/index.trl"               // hope, despair, courage
import "trl/modules/emotion_dynamics.trl"     // [#Despairing], [#Hopeful], the despair <-> hope thread

// Lateral thematic links (optional, machine-followable — for discovery / embeddings).
assoc hope_bringer -> [
  despair_event_horizon : "the restoring inverse of (turns despair where it forecloses)",
  rousing_speech        : "the figure-by-presence cousin of the speech-by-oratory",
  the_paragon           : "an upright Hope Bringer is also the moral",
  hope                  : "rekindles",
  courage               : "leads the broken back into",
  despair               : "the [#Despairing] he turns"
]


// === ONTOLOGY ===
// The beacon-figure: living proof one figure evens the odds (the Ace, the Chosen, the Rebel Leader).
imply HopeBringer -> [Beacon, Inspiring, Heroic, Narrative]


// === ABSTRACT RULE ===
// Naming rule (the inverse of the Despair Event Horizon): a beacon-figure whose DEED reaches the
// [#Despairing] turns them — despair is dropped, hope and resolve restored, and the broken are led
// back toward the fight. By PRESENCE/DEEDS, not oratory: the figure is a [+Beacon] and the event is
// his deed aimed at the despairing ones ($d), no band / cause oration in the signature.
rule Hope_Bringer {
  when:
    char $h [+Beacon]
    evt  $deed [&Rallies(agent=$h, target=$d)]
    $d [#Despairing]
  then:
    $d [-Despairing]
    $d [#Hopeful]
    $d [+Resolved]
    $d -- hope
    $d -- courage
}


// === CONCRETE VIGNETTE: Joan of Arc at the Siege of Orléans (military history, 1429) ===
// The English have held the siege for months; the French garrison is beaten, sick of losing, and
// sure the war is lost. A teenage peasant girl arrives claiming a divine mandate — and it is not a
// speech that turns them. It is her: she rides the walls under fire, plants her banner at the
// assaults, takes an arrow through the shoulder and returns to the line the same day. By her deeds
// and her presence the demoralized garrison is remade into an army that believes it can win — and
// within days they lift a siege that had stood for seven months.

// THE MAID OF ORLÉANS — the beacon, living proof the odds can be evened
char joan [+Protagonist] [+Beacon]
joan [+Chosen] [+Devoted_To(target=france)]

// THE ORLÉANS GARRISON — the broken, beaten defenders
char garrison [+Collective] [#Despairing]

// EXT. THE BOULEVART OF LES TOURELLES - DAY
set les_tourelles [+Exterior] [+Day]
les_tourelles [+Contested]

scene the_relief {
  beat 1 {
    joan @ les_tourelles
    garrison @ les_tourelles
    // Not a speech — the deed: wounded at the assault, she pulls the arrow and goes back to the line.
    evt the_assault [&Rallies(agent=joan, target=garrison)]
        dialog(inject=[speaker=joan], inline="""
               speaker: "{speaker}"
               cue: "an English bolt through her shoulder, the banner taken up again, back at the ditch"
               tone: unflinching, certain
               text: "All is yours — go in! When my banner touches the wall, the place is yours."
               """)
    // Hope_Bringer fires (the inverse of the Despair Event Horizon):
    garrison [-Despairing]
    garrison [#Hopeful]
    garrison [+Resolved]
    garrison -- hope
    garrison -- courage
  }
}
